# The current Chrome extension uses browser-managed user OAuth.
# It does not read this file and must never ship a service-account private key.
# extension/manifest.json already contains the permanent public key and matching
# public Chrome Extension OAuth client ID. Keep those values unchanged when
# sharing or updating the extension; do not put OAuth configuration here.
# Never place an access token or client secret in this file.
#
# A future optional backend may add its own documented configuration here. Do
# not place Google access tokens, private keys, or client inventory in this
# repository.
